<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions 13.46 bln rupees' bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions 13.46 bln rupees' bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month short-term federal bonds worth 13.46 billion rupees on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank received bids worth 18,138.905 million rupees, out of which bids worth 13,463.905 million rupees were accepted at a weighted average yield of 16.46165 percent per annum, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.62 rupees) -- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
